@model AccountabilityPreviewViewModel
<details class="accountability-panel" open="@(!Model.Editable)" id="snap-workout" data-snap-panel><summary>Snap Workouts</summary>
<section class="snap-workout" data-snap-workout>
    <div class="accountability-heading"><div><p class="accountability-tag">QUICK ASSIGNMENT</p><h3>Snap Workout</h3></div><a class="button" asp-controller="AccountabilityPreview" asp-action="Snap" asp-route-clientId="@Model.ClientId">Open in client portal →</a></div>
    <details><summary>Rates &amp; completion rules</summary><p>Assign exercises with sets, reps and weight. Rates apply to prescribed completed or incomplete reps or sets. Separate completion and extra-rep rewards can be added alongside unfinished-work penalties. On-time completion is required for these rewards; new max-weight assignments count reps within their weight limit. Earlier assignments retain their prescribed-weight requirements.</p></details>
    @if (Model.Editable || Model.CanAssignSnap)
    {
        <details class="snap-editor" open><summary>Create Snap Workout</summary>
        <form data-snap-assign>
            <div class="accountability-fields"><label>Workout name<input name="snapName" maxlength="100" value="Snap Workout" required /></label><label>Assignment date<input name="snapDate" type="date" required /></label><label>Completion deadline<input name="snapDeadline" type="datetime-local" required /></label><label>Assessment cap per workout ($)<input name="snapCap" type="number" min="0" max="10000" step=".01" value="100" required /></label></div>
            <p data-snap-deadline-zone></p><p>The deadline defaults to two hours after assignment. Late results forfeit completion and extra-rep rewards; unfinished-work penalties use reviewed final quantities. Unknown results remain pending.</p>
            <p>The cap applies separately to this workout’s total fines and total incentives. Assignment rates and targets become part of the client’s approval terms.</p>
            <h3>Exercises</h3><p>Type each exercise below. Enter the heaviest permitted weight in lb; use 0 lb for bodyweight movements. Qualifying sets must meet the reps target without exceeding the weight limit.</p>
            <div class="snap-simple-exercises" data-snap-draft></div>
            <p><button type="button" data-snap-add>Add another exercise</button></p>
            <p data-snap-catalog-status role="status"></p>
            <button type="submit">Assign Snap Workout</button>
        </form></details>
        <details class="snap-library"><summary>Assign from past Snap Workouts</summary>
            <p>Check one or more workouts, choose a new date and deadline, then assign. Each copy keeps its original exercises, targets, rates and cap. Results are not copied.</p>
            <form data-snap-reuse>
                <div class="accountability-fields"><label>Assignment date<input name="reuseDate" type="date" required /></label><label>Completion deadline<input name="reuseDeadline" type="datetime-local" required /></label></div>
                <p data-reuse-zone></p><div data-snap-library></div>
                <p data-snap-library-status role="status"></p><button type="submit">Assign selected workouts</button>
            </form>
        </details>

    }
    <p data-snap-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div data-snap-assignments></div>
    <p data-snap-weekly-total></p>
    <p class="snap-preview-note">Selected-week calculated totals. Assignments and completion records are saved securely for the connected coach and client. No payment is collected automatically.</p>
</section>
</details>
